\begin{definition}
\label{def:7-47-extra-1}




A Lie group homomorphism $F:G\to H$ is a smooth group homomorphism. It is a Lie group isomorphism when it is a diffeomorphism (then $F^{-1}$ is also a homomorphism).
\end{definition}

